# Quiz Component for the Crash Course

## Finish line

Pinned 2026-07-24 by [Pin the finish line](./pin-the-finish-line.svx).

- Matt authors `<Quiz><QuizQuestion data={{ … }} /></Quiz>` **inline** in an AI
  Coding Crash Course lesson body, with the question, choices, `correct`, and the
  explanation all in the object literal. No second authoring step, no separate
  record to create first.
- That markup survives the Course Video Manager → Dropbox `/course.json` v3 →
  course-sync path unchanged, with no manifest schema change.
- A learner — **including a logged-out one** — answers in the lesson body, and
  immediately sees whether they were right plus the authored explanation.
- Each answer writes a `QuestionResponse` row carrying
  `fields: { answer, correct }`, keyed by a minted survey session id
  (`respondentKey` / `surveySessionId`), upgrading to `userId` /
  `emailListSubscriberId` when identity resolves.
- Correct/incorrect rates are queryable per question without parsing lesson
  bodies.
- **Maintained after ship:** one entry point documents the MDX component, the
  answer endpoint contract, and the `fields` shape, so the next person does not
  have to trace three repos to find out how a quiz works.

## Vocabulary

- **quiz** — a set of questions that have correct answers and grade the learner.
  Distinct from a survey, which collects opinions and has no correctness.
- **survey** — the existing AI Hero / course-builder system for collecting
  learner answers with no notion of right or wrong.
- **crash course** — settled 2026-07-24: the **draft AI Coding Crash Course**,
  sync binding `csb_ai_coding_crash_course`, anchor workshop `workshop-2ozd9`.
  Not the public AI SDK v6 Crash Course.
- **inline authoring** — the quiz question and its answer key live in the
  lesson's MDX body, not in a separate record. Settled 2026-07-24 as the chosen
  model.
- **data-driven authoring** — quiz content as a content resource with MDX
  carrying only a reference. Considered and rejected; see Out of scope.
- **grading** — deciding whether one submitted answer matches that question's
  `correct` value. Per-question, client-side, already implemented in
  `@coursebuilder/survey`. Distinct from scoring.
- **scoring** — an aggregate result across a set of questions. Does not exist
  anywhere today and is not in the finish line.
- **survey session id** — the minted anonymous identifier written to
  `QuestionResponse.respondentKey` / `surveySessionId`. This effort is the first
  writer of those columns, so it defines what they mean.

## Notes

- Domain: AI Hero app (`~/Code/badass-courses/ai-hero`, `apps/ai-hero`) plus the
  course-builder monorepo (`~/Code/badass-courses/course-builder`, notably
  `packages/survey`, `packages/adapter-drizzle`, `packages/ui`).
- Source of the request: Matt Pocock in Slack `#cc-matt-p`, thread
  `https://eggheadio.slack.com/archives/C0211NSK3TP/p1784717959599139`
  (2026-07-24). Tagged `:shitrat:` on the root.
- What Matt asked for, verbatim in substance:
  - A `<Quiz>` component for the crash course, text-based questions only.
  - Persisted answers preferred; `localStorage` explicitly acceptable to him.
  - It must work inline in the lesson body.
  - Shape `<Quiz><QuizQuestion data={} /></Quiz>`, with the question and answer
    baked in so there is "no extra thing to author" — this makes it easy for his
    agent to generate and edit quizzes.
  - "Yep as long as I've got an API for it I'm OK."
- What Joel said in the thread: the survey system already is quizzes; an MDX
  component may need wiring but "the hard bits are done/baked in"; it is data
  driven, content resources, over the same API.
- Open tension to grill: Matt wants content inline in MDX, Joel wants content
  resources over the API. Matt's last message suggests an API satisfies him, but
  that has not been confirmed against his authoring loop.
- Skills to consult: `grill-me`, `herdr-orchestration`, `prototype`.
- **Execution authorization (Joel, 2026-07-24): granted, gated on one prototype.**
  Sessions decide until a throwaway `<Quiz>` exists that Joel can actually click
  in a lesson body. Once he has touched it and said it feels right, sessions are
  authorized to build the real component, the answer endpoint, and the MDX
  registration. Until then, decisions only.
- Mid-effort call (Joel, 2026-07-24): the multi-select grading bug in
  `@coursebuilder/survey` gets fixed in the package as separate work, not folded
  into this effort. See the chartered step for how the inline quiz behaves in the
  meantime.
- Version constraint: AI Hero pins `@coursebuilder/survey@^1.0.5`; package source
  is at `1.0.13`. A package fix does not reach AI Hero without moving the pin.

## Decision ledger

- [Trace the course-builder survey primitives](./trace-coursebuilder-survey-primitives.svx)
  — `@coursebuilder/survey` is a quiz engine named "survey": machine id is
  `quizMachine`, questions carry `correct` + `answer`, and the machine grades into
  `answered.correct`/`incorrect`/`neutral`. Five gaps to a real quiz, including a
  multi-select grading bug that accepts a proper subset as fully correct.
- [Trace the AI Hero survey system end to end](./trace-ai-hero-survey-system.svx)
  — Surveys and questions are `contentResource` rows joined by
  `contentResourceResource`; answers are `QuestionResponse.fields.answer` mirrored
  to Kit. The REST API covers surveys only: **there is no question CRUD endpoint**,
  and the admin form does not expose `correct`. No supported path can author a
  graded question today.
- [Trace AI Hero MDX rendering and the crash course](./trace-ai-hero-mdx-and-crash-course.svx)
  — Lesson bodies compile through `next-mdx-remote/rsc` at request time with
  `blockJS: false`. Structured object props work (`ThemeImage urls={{...}}` ships
  today), stateful client components work, and no quiz component is registered.
  Crash-course content flows Course Video Manager → Dropbox `/course.json` →
  course-sync, whose v3 schema carries `body` strings and rejects extra properties.
- [Pin the finish line](./pin-the-finish-line.svx) — inline MDX authoring with
  server-side answers; draft AI Coding Crash Course; anonymous learners keyed by a
  minted survey session id; `fields: { answer, correct }`; grading machine reused
  but fresh UI; multi-select bug fixed separately; build authorized after one
  prototype.

## Latent

- Whether quiz answers should feed the existing subscriber/segmentation
  machinery the surveys feed, or stay inert learner-facing state. Surveys mirror
  answers to Kit subscriber fields today; nobody has said whether quizzes should.
- Whether the component eventually graduates from AI Hero into a
  `@coursebuilder/*` primitive other apps inherit.
- How quiz content stays correct as course content changes — the answer key lives
  in a lesson body that Matt's agent rewrites.
- Whether aggregate scoring ("you got 7 of 10") is ever wanted. Explicitly not in
  this finish line.
- **`correct` silently forces choice shuffling.** `loadQuestion` shuffles whenever
  `correct` or `shuffleChoices` is set, with no opt-out
  (`packages/survey/src/survey-machine.ts:57-60`). Found while building the
  prototype. Authored choice order is never honored on a graded question, so an
  author writing "all of the above" last gets a surprise. Decide whether the real
  component needs an escape hatch.
- Dead surfaces found during the trace, to be cleaned up or logged separately:
  the commented-out published-state check on `/survey/[slug]`
  (`page.tsx:47-51`), `deleteSurvey` orphaning question resources and responses
  (`surveys-query.ts:151-173`), and the unimported analytics provider
  (`lib/analytics/providers/survey.ts:9-24`).

## Out of scope

- **Question CRUD in the REST API.** No endpoint exists for question
  create/update/delete/attach/reorder — only server actions behind the admin UI.
  Inline authoring means Matt never needs it, so building it sits past the finish
  line. Revisit only if the content-resource model is ever chosen.
- **Adding `correct` / `answer` controls to the admin question form.** Same
  reason: the answer key lives in MDX now, not in the admin CRUD path.
- **The content-resource quiz model** (`<Quiz id="…" />` referencing DB rows).
  Considered and rejected in [Pin the finish line](./pin-the-finish-line.svx)
  because it does not ride course-sync and would force Matt to author quizzes out
  of band from how his course content actually moves.
- **Fixing the multi-select grading bug in `@coursebuilder/survey`.** Real bug
  affecting existing surveys, but it is package work with its own release and pin
  move. Ruled out of this effort by Joel, 2026-07-24.
- **Aggregate quiz scoring.** No score state exists in any machine today and the
  finish line does not ask for one.
